{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790266488,"nonce":"cZzM8IDTCd/tGTNTSO7p0x04Fh4=","message":"Revised 2026-09-24 (Luis): `gui` stays the HTTP surface, but the framing changes with flows calling views rather than returning specs. `git work gui` runs flows in its own process and selects an HTML backend for the very same `work.view.*` calls the terminal renders, so the two surfaces remain two backends of one capability and no capability exists on one and not the other. The spec `{\"view\",\"bindings\",\"items\"}` is still the wire form: `--gui` on `view` and `flow run` serializes the call and sends it to the gui, which is exactly the headless path a non-TTY run takes when it prints the spec to stdout. A backend missing a view kind fails naming itself, unchanged. The rename itself (webui -\u003e gui, no `tui` command) is untouched by this. Design: doc/design/config-entity.md E9 and doc/design/cli-convention.md.","files":null}]}